# Git stores every source file in this repo with LF endings: the Dart and
# Serverpod generators write LF. On Windows a clone with `core.autocrlf=true`
# checks those files out as CRLF, so the next time a generator rewrites one with
# LF, git reports it as modified even though the bytes are identical.
# Pinning the worktree to LF keeps `git status` quiet on every platform.
#
# In an existing clone, refresh the cached stat data once after pulling this
# file:  git add --renormalize .

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary content.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
